{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/705", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 705. Exterior Walls 705.1 to 705.4 {As in IBC} 705.5 Fire-resistance ratings. 705.5.1 Exterior walls. Exterior walls shall be fire resistance rated in accordance with Table 601, based on the type of construction, and Table 705.5, based on the fire separation distance. The required fire-resistance rating of exterior walls with a fire separation distance of greater than10 feet (3048 mm) shall be rated for exposure to fire from the inside. The required fire-resistance rating of exterior walls with a fire separation distance of less than or equal to 10 feet (3048 mm) shall be rated for exposure to fire from both sides. 705.5.2 Porch roofs \u2013 Abutting. In new construction, renovation, or replacement of a porch roof that abuts another porch roof fire-retardant-treated wood sheathing shall be installed. 705.6 to 705.11 {As in IBC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "705", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|II|7|705", "title": "Section 705. Exterior Walls", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/705"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/706", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 706. Fire Walls 706.1 to 706.8 {As in IBC} 706.9 Penetrations. Penetrations through fire walls must comply with \u00a7 714 {\"Penetrations\"} of this Code. Penetrations through party walls are not allowed. 706.10 to 706.11 {As in IBC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "706", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|II|7|706", "title": "Section 706. Fire Walls", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/706"}
