{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 3306. Protection of Pedestrians {As in IBC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "3306", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|II|33|3306", "title": "Section 3306. Protection of Pedestrians\n{As in IBC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/3306"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/3307", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 3307. Protection of Adjoining Property 3307.1 Protection required. {As in IBC} 3307.2 Shared elements \u2013 General. Repairs to elements shared by a demolished or moved structure and an adjoining structure must comply with all applicable provisions of this Code. 3307.3 Shared elements \u2013 Walls. Party walls must be repaired and finished by the owner of the demolished or moved structure. The repairs must include: 1. restoration or replacement of any flashing on adjoining property that has been broken or damaged during the operations, 2. removal of all plaster from the exposed side of the wall, and 3. cleaning and finishing the wall with approved waterproof material. ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "3307", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|II|33|3307", "title": "Section 3307. Protection of Adjoining Property", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/3307"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/II/3308to3313", "_type": "page"}}
