{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/III/250.68", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 250.68. Grounding Electrode Conductor and Bonding Jumper Connection to Grounding Electrodes. {Introductory Paragraph as in NEC} (A) Accessibility. The connection of a grounding electrode conductor or bonding jumper conductor to a grounding electrode must be: (1) ahead of all turnoff valves and unions, and (2) accessible. Exceptions : {As in NEC} (B) Effective Grounding Path. {As in NEC} (C) Grounding Electrode Connections. {As in NEC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "250.68", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|III|2|250|250.68", "title": "Section 250.68. Grounding Electrode Conductor and Bonding Jumper Connection to Grounding Electrodes. {Introductory Paragraph as in NEC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/III/250.68"}
