{"body": "Baltimore City Code Part IV International Fuel Gas Code \u00a7 4-101. City adoption \u00a7 4-102. City modifications. Chapter 1 Scope and Administration \u00a7\u00a7 101 \u2013 116 Chapter 2 Definitions \u00a7\u00a7 201 \u2013 202 Chapter 3 General Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 301 \u2013 307 Chapter 4 Gas Piping Installations \u00a7\u00a7 405 \u2013 405 Chapter 5 Chimneys and Vents [As in IFGC] Chapter 6 Specific Appliances \u00a7\u00a7 621 \u2013 621 Chapter 7 Gaseous Hydrogen Systems [As in IFGC] Chapter 8 Referenced Standards [As in IFGC] Attachments", "num": "IV", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV", "title": "Part IV International Fuel Gas Code", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/4-101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 4-101. City adoption (a) In general. The International Fuel Gas Code (2021 Edition) is adopted as part of the Building, Fire, and Related Codes of Baltimore City, subject to the additions, deletions, amendments, and other modifications contained in this Part IV. (b) Codification. Unless otherwise specified, chapter and section numbers in this Part IV refer to the chapter and section numbers of the International Fuel Gas Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "4-101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|4-101", "title": "\u00a7 4-101. City adoption", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/4-101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/4-102", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 4-102. City modifications. The additions, deletions, amendments, and other modifications adopted by the City are as follows: ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "4-102", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|4-102", "title": "\u00a7 4-102. City modifications.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/4-102"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 1 Scope and Administration Section 101. General Section 102. Applicability {As in IFGC} Section 103. Department of Inspection Section 104. Duties and Powers of Code Official Section 105. Approval Section 106. Permits Section 107. Construction Documents {As in IFGC} Section 108. Notice of Approval {As in IFGC} Section 109. Fees {As in IFGC} Section 110. Service Utilities {As in IFGC} Section 111. Temporary Equipment, Systems, and Uses {As in IFGC} Section 112. Inspections and Testing {As in IFGC} Section 113. Administrative and Judicial Review Section 114. Board of Appeals {Not Adopted} Section 115. Violations Section 116. Stop Work Order", "num": "1", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1", "title": "Chapter 1 Scope and Administration", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 101. General 101.1 Title. The regulations contained in this Code constitute and are known as the \"Baltimore City Fuel Gas Code \". 101.1.1 References to \"this Code\". Throughout this Part IV, all references to \"this Code\" refer to the Baltimore City Fuel Gas Code . 101.2 to 101.5 {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|101", "title": "Section 101. General", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/102", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 102. Applicability {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "102", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|102", "title": "Section 102. Applicability\n{As in IFGC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/102"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/103", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 103. Department of Inspection 103.1 General. This Code is administered and enforced by the Department of Housing and Community Development and its Commissioner. Accordingly, in this Code: 1. \"Department of Inspection\" or \"Department\" means the Department of Housing and Community Development, and 2. \"Code Official\", means the Building Official, as defined in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . 103.2 to 103.3 {Not Adopted} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "103", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|103", "title": "Section 103. Department of Inspection", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/103"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/104", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 104. Duties and Powers of Code Official 104.1 to 104.2 {As in IFGC} 104.3 Inspections. The Code Official must make all of the required inspections or accept reports of inspection by approved agencies or individuals. All reports of these inspections must be in writing and signed by a responsible officer of the approved agency or by the responsible individual. The Code Official may engage any expert opinion that the Code Official considers necessary to report on unusual technical issues that arise. 104.4 Right of entry. The Code Official may enter any structure or premises at reasonable times to inspect, subject to constitutional restrictions on unreasonable searches and seizures. If entry is refused or not obtained, the Code Official may pursue recourse as provided by law, including \u00a7 104 {\"... Powers of Building Official\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 104.5 Identification. {As in IFGC} 104.6 Notices and orders. The Code Official may issue all notices or orders necessary to ensure compliance with this Code. 104.7 Department records. The Code Official must keep records of all of the Department's business and activities under this Code. 104.8 Liability. {Not Adopted. See State Courts Article \u00a7 5-302} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "104", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|104", "title": "Section 104. Duties and Powers of Code Official", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/104"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/105", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 105. Approval 105.1 Modifications. {As in IFGC} 105.2 Alternative materials and methods. The provisions of this Code are not intended to prevent the installation of any material or to prohibit any method of construction not specifically prescribed by this Code, as long as that alternative has been approved. An alternative material or method of construction may be approved if the Code Official finds in writing that, for the purpose intended: 1. the proposed alternative is satisfactory and complies with the intent of this Code, and 2. the material, method, or work offered is at least the equivalent of that prescribed in this Code in quality, strength, effectiveness, fire resistance, durability, and safety. 105.2.1 Research reports. {As in IFGC} 105.3 to 105.5 {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "105", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|105", "title": "Section 105. Approval", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/105"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/106", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 106. Permits 106.1 to 106.2 {As in IFGC} 106.3 Application for permit. The requirements for obtaining a permit are as set forth in \u00a7 105.3 {\"Application for permit\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 106.3.1 to 106.3.2 {Not Adopted} 106.4 Preliminary inspection. {As in IFGC} 106.5 Permit issuance. {As in IFGC} 106.5.1 to 106.5.2 {As in IFGC} 106.5.3 Expiration. Unless extended, a permit expires as set forth in \u00a7 105.5 {\"Expiration; Extension\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 106.5.4 Extension. A permit may be extended as provided in \u00a7 105.5 {\"Expiration; Extension\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 106.5.5 Suspension or revocation. The Building Official may suspend or revoke a permit as provided in \u00a7 105.6 {\"Suspension or revocation\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 106.5.6 to 106.5.7 {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "106", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|106", "title": "Section 106. Permits", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/106"}
