{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/115", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 115. Violations 115.1 to 115.3 {As in IFGC} 115.4 Violation penalties. The penalties for a violation of this Code are as provided in \u00a7 114 {\"Violations\u201d} of the Baltimore City Building Code for a violation of that Code. 115.5 to 115.6 {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "115", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|115", "title": "Section 115. Violations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/115"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/116", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 116. Stop Work Order 116.1 General. The issuance and enforcement of stop-work orders are as provided in \u00a7 115 {\"Stop-Work Order\u201d} of the Baltimore City Building Code. 116.2 to 116.4 {Not Adopted} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "116", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|1|116", "title": "Section 116. Stop Work Order", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/116"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 2 Definitions Section 201. General Section 202. General Definitions", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|2", "title": "Chapter 2 Definitions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 201. General 201.1 to 201.2 {As in IFGC} 201.3 Terms defined in other codes. If a term is not defined in this Code and is defined in the Baltimore City Building Code or in one or another of the standards and codes listed in \u00a7 101.4 {\"Referenced Codes\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code , the term has the meaning given to it in that code or standard. 201.4 Terms not defined. {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|2|201", "title": "Section 201. General", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 202. General Definitions 202.1 General. Except as provided in \u00a7 202.2 of this Code, terms that are used in this Code and defined in the International Fuel Gas Code (2021 Edition) have the meanings given in the International Fuel Gas Code (2021 Edition). 202.2 Supplemental definitions Notwithstanding any different definition in the International Fuel Gas Code , the following terms have the meanings given in this \u00a7 202.2. 202.2.1 Building. \"Building\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . 202.2.2 Code Official. \"Code Official\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 103.1 of this Code. 202.2.3 Design-flood elevation. {Not Adopted} 202.2.4 Flood Hazard Area. \"Flood Hazard Area\" means a Regulated Flood Hazard Area established under and regulated by the Floodplain Management Code. 202.2.5 Floodplain Management Code. \"Floodplain Management Code\" means the Baltimore City Floodplain Management Code, City Code Article 7 {\"Natural Resources\"}, Division I {\"Floodplain Management\"}. 202.2.6 May not, etc. \"May not\", \"must not\", and \"no ... may\" are each mandatory negative terms used to establish a prohibition. 202.2.7 Must/shall. \"Must\" and \"shall\" are each mandatory terms used to express a requirement or to impose a duty. 202.2.8 Occupancy. \"Occupancy\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . 202.2.9 Premises. \"Premises\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|2|202", "title": "Section 202. General Definitions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 3 General Regulations Section 301. General Sections 302 to 306. {As in IFGC} Section 307. Condensate Disposal Sections 308 to 310. {As in IFGC}", "num": "3", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|3", "title": "Chapter 3 General Regulations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/301", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 301. General 301.1 to 301.10 {As in IFGC} 301.11 Flood hazard areas. In a flood hazard area, the appliance, equipment, and system installations regulated by this code must be located at or above the elevation required by the Floodplain Management Code for electric, plumbing, and mechanical systems and their attendant components and equipment. Exception: {Not Adopted} 301.12 to 301.15 {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "301", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|3|301", "title": "Section 301. General", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/301"}
