{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 302 to 306. {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "302 to 306", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|3|302to306", "title": "Sections 302 to 306. {As in IFGC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/302to306"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/307", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 307. Condensate Disposal 307.1 Evaporators and cooling coils. {As in IFGC} 307.2 Fuel-burning appliances. {As in IFGC} 307.2.1 Discharge. Condensate may not discharge into a street, alley, or other area so as to cause a nuisance. Clear water discharge must be conveyed to the storm drain where feasible unless otherwise approved by the Code Official. 307.3 Drain pipe material and sizes. {As in IFGC} 307.4 Traps. {Not Adopted} 307.5 Auxiliary drain pan. {As in IFGC} 307.6 Condensate pumps. {As in IFGC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "307", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IV|3|307", "title": "Section 307. Condensate Disposal", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IV/307"}
