{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1206. Piping Installation 1206.1 to 1206.8 {As in IMC} 1206.9 Strains and stresses {As in IMC} 1206.9.1 Flood hazard areas. Piping located in a flood hazard area must be capable of resisting hydrostatic and hydrodynamic loads and stresses, including the effects of buoyancy, as required by the Floodplain Management Code. . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1206", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|V|12|1206", "title": "Section 1206. Piping Installation", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/V/1206"}
