{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 2 Definitions Section 201. General Section 202. General Definitions", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|2", "title": "Chapter 2 Definitions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 201. General 201.1 to 201.2 {As in IPC} 201.3 Terms defined in other codes. If a term is not defined in this Code and is defined in the Baltimore City Building Code or in one or another of the standards and codes listed in \u00a7 101.4 {\"Referenced Codes\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code , the term has the meaning given to it in that code or standard. 201.4 Terms not defined. {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|2|201", "title": "Section 201. General", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 202. General Definitions 202.1 General. Except as provided in \u00a7 202.2 of this Code, terms that are used in this Code and defined in the International Plumbing Code (2021 Edition) have the meanings given in the International Plumbing Code (2021 Edition). 202.2 Supplemental definitions. Notwithstanding any different definition in the International Plumbing Code , the following terms have the meanings given in this \u00a7 202.2. 202.2.1 Building. \"Building\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . 202.2.2 Code Official. \"Code Official\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 103.1 of this Code. 202.2.3 Design-flood elevation. {Not Adopted} 202.2.4 Flood Hazard Area. \"Flood Hazard Area\" means a Regulated Flood Hazard Area established under and regulated by the Baltimore City Floodplain Management Code, City Code Article 7 {\"Natural Resources\"}, Division I {\"Floodplain Management\"} 202.2.5 May not, etc. \"May not\", \"must not\", and \"no ... may\" are each mandatory negative terms used to establish a prohibition. 202.2.6 Must/shall. \"Must\" and \"shall\" are each mandatory terms used to express a requirement or to impose a duty. 202.2.7 Occupancy. \"Occupancy\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|2|202", "title": "Section 202. General Definitions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 3 General Regulations Sections 301 to 304. {As in IPC} Section 305. Protection of Pipes and Plumbing System Components Sections 306 to 308. {As in IPC} Section 309. Flood Hazard Resistance Sections 310 to 313. {As in IPC} Section 314. Condensate Disposal Section 315. Penetrations {As in IPC} Section 316. Alternative Engineered Design {As in IPC} Section 317. Connection to Water and Sewer Systems", "num": "3", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3", "title": "Chapter 3 General Regulations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/301to304", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 301 to 304. {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "301 to 304", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|301to304", "title": "Sections 301 to 304. {As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/301to304"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/305", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 305. Protection of Pipes and Plumbing System Components 305.1 to 305.3 {As in IPC} 305.4 Freezing or overheating. The plumbing system must be protected from freezing or overheating. 305.4.1 Specific requirements. The following conditions must be met: 1. Water service piping must be installed below recorded frost lines. Earth cover above the top of the pipe must be at least 36 inches (914 mm). 2. Earth cover above the top of building sewers that connect to public sewage systems or to individual sewage disposal systems must be at least 30 inches (762 mm). 3. In systems that are used seasonally, water piping must have provisions for draining. 4. Piping must be installed so that the contents will not be heated due to close proximity to any heat source or from direct solar radiation. 5. All drain piping and water piping installed in exterior walls, attics, and other areas exposed to outdoor temperatures must be protected from freezing. In heated spaces, the piping must be installed on the heated side of the building insulation. 305.5 to 305.7 {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "305", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|305", "title": "Section 305. Protection of Pipes and Plumbing System Components", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/305"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/306to308", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 306 to 308. {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "306 to 308", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|306to308", "title": "Sections 306 to 308. {As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/306to308"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/309", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 309. Flood Hazard Resistance 309.1 General. In a flood hazard area, plumbing systems must be constructed, located, and installed in accordance with the requirements of the Baltimore City Floodplain Management Code, City Code Article 7 {\"Natural Resources\"} , Division I {\"Floodplain Management\"}. 309.2 Scope. The requirements of this \u00a7 309 apply to all plumbing systems, their attendant components and equipment, including the following: 1. all water service pipes, 2. pump seals in individual water supply systems, 3. Covers on potable water wells, 4. all sanitary drainage piping, 5. all storm drainage piping, 6. manhole covers, 7. all other plumbing fixtures, faucets, fixture fittings, piping systems, and equipment, 8. water heaters, and 9. vents and vent systems. Exception: {Not adopted} 309.3 Coastal high-hazard area and coastal A zones. {Not Adopted} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "309", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|309", "title": "Section 309. Flood Hazard Resistance", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/309"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/310to313", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 310 to 313. {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "310 to 313", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|310to313", "title": "Sections 310 to 313. {As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/310to313"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/314", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 314. Condensate Disposal 314.1 Fuel burning appliances. {As in IPC} 314.2 Evaporators and cooling coils. {As in IPC} 314.2.1 Condensate disposal. Condensate from all cooling coils or evaporators must be conveyed from the drain pan outlet to an approved place of disposal. The piping must maintain a minimum horizontal slope in the direction of discharge of not less than one-eighth unit vertical in 12 units horizontal (1% slope). Condensate may not discharge into a street, alley, or other area so as to cause a nuisance. Clear water discharge must be conveyed to the storm drain where feasible unless otherwise approved by the Code Official. 314.2.2 to 314.2.5 {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "314", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|314", "title": "Section 314. Condensate Disposal", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/314"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/315", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 315. Penetrations {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "315", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|315", "title": "Section 315. Penetrations\n{As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/315"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/316", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 316. Alternative Engineered Design {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "316", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|316", "title": "Section 316. Alternative Engineered Design\n{As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/316"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/317", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 317. Connection to Water and Sewer Systems 317.1 Availability of Public Water and Sewer. The water distribution and sewer system of any building in which plumbing fixtures are installed must be connected to a public water supply system and to a public sewer system unless otherwise authorized by a National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System permit issued under Title 9 of the State Environment Article. Private septic tank systems may only be installed with the written permission of the Code Official. 317.2 Private Systems. Private systems must comply with COMAR 26.04.02 {\"Sewage Disposal and Certain Water Systems...\"}. ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "317", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|3|317", "title": "Section 317. Connection to Water and Sewer Systems", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/317"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 4 Fixtures, Faucets, and Fixture Fittings Sections 401 to 405. {As in IPC} Section 406. Automatic Clothes Washers Sections 407 to 426. {As in IPC}", "num": "4", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|4", "title": "Chapter 4 Fixtures, Faucets, and Fixture Fittings", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/401to405", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 401 to 405. {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "401 to 405", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|4|401to405", "title": "Sections 401 to 405. {As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/401to405"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/406", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 406. Automatic Clothes Washers 406.1 to 406.2 {As in IPC} 406.3 Drip pan. If a clothes washer is to be installed in a location where leakage can cause structural damage to the building, the washer must be installed over a drip pan in accordance with the manufacturer's instructions. The pan drain must extend full size and terminate over a suitably located indirect waste receptor or floor drain. ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "406", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|4|406", "title": "Section 406. Automatic Clothes Washers", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/406"}
