{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/8", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 8 Indirect/Special Waste Section 801. General {As in IPC} Section 802. Indirect Wastes Section 803. Special Wastes {As in IPC}", "num": "8", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|8", "title": "Chapter 8 Indirect/Special Waste", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/8"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/801", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 801. General {As in IPC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "801", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|8|801", "title": "Section 801. General\n{As in IPC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/801"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/802", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 802. Indirect Wastes 802.1 Where required. {As in IPC} 802.1.1 to 802.1.5 {As in IPC} 802.1.6 Commercial dishwashing machines. {As in IPC} 802.1.6.1 No discharge through grease interceptor. Commercial dishwashers are not permitted to discharge through a grease interceptor. 802.1.7 Food utensils, dishes, pots, and pans sink. {As in IPC} 802.2 to 802.4 {As in IPC} 802.5 Wading and Toddler Pools. All wading pools and toddler pools must be equipped with 2 drains from a single drain line so as not to create a vacuum if either of the drains is covered. The drainage must discharge indirectly through an air gap to a trapped and vented receptor. ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "802", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VI|8|802", "title": "Section 802. Indirect Wastes", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/802"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VI/803", "_type": "page"}}
