{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VIII/1203", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1203. Emergency and Standby Power Systems 1203.1 General. {As in IFC} 1203.1.1 to 1203.1.2 {As in IFC} 1203.1.3 Installation. Emergency and standby power systems must be installed in accordance with the National Electrical Code , NFPA 110, and NFPA 111. Existing installations must be maintained in accordance with the original approval. 1203.1.4 to 1203.1.9 {As in IFC} 1203.2 to 1203.6 {As in IFC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1203", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VIII|12|1203", "title": "Section 1203. Emergency and Standby Power Systems", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VIII/1203"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VIII/1204", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1204. Solar Photovoltaic Power Systems 1204.1 General {As in IFC} 1204.2 Access and pathways. {As in IFC} 1204.2.1 Solar photovoltaic systems for Group R-3 buildings. Solar photovoltaic systems for Group R-3 buildings must comply with \u00a7\u00a7 1204.2.1.1 through 1204.2.1.3. Exceptions: {Not Adopted} 1204.2.1.1 to 1204.2.1.3 {As in IFC} 1204.2.2 Emergency escape and rescue openings. {As in IFC} 1204.3 to 1204.5 {As in IFC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1204", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|VIII|12|1204", "title": "Section 1204. Solar Photovoltaic Power Systems", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/VIII/1204"}
