{"body": "Baltimore City Code Part IX-B International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Residential Provisions \u00a7 9B-101. City adoption. \u00a7 9B-102. City modifications. Chapter 1 Scope and Administration \u00a7\u00a7 101 \u2013 113 Chapter 2 Definitions \u00a7\u00a7 201 \u2013 202 Chapter 3 General Requirements [As in IECC-R] Chapter 4 Residential Energy Efficiency \u00a7\u00a7 406 \u2013 406 Chapter 5 Existing Buildings [As in IECC-R] Chapter 6 Referenced Standards [As in IECC-R] Attachments", "num": "IX-B", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B", "title": "Part IX-B International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Residential Provisions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/9B-101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9B-101. City adoption. (a) In general. The International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Residential Provisions (2018 Edition) is adopted as part of the Building, Fire, and Related Codes of Baltimore City, subject to the additions, deletions, amendments, and other modifications contained in this Part IX-B. (b) Codification. Unless otherwise specified, chapter and section numbers in this Part IX-B refer to the chapter and section numbers of the International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Residential Provisions. ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "9B-101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|9B-101", "title": "\u00a7 9B-101. City adoption.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/9B-101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/9B-102", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9B-102. City modifications. The additions, deletions, amendments, and other modifications adopted by the City are as follows: ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "9B-102", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|9B-102", "title": "\u00a7 9B-102. City modifications.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/9B-102"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 1 Scope and Administration {MBPS Modifications \u2013 Additional requirements concerning energy conservation for structures may be found in the Energy Conservation Building Standards, State Public Utility Companies Article \u00a7\u00a7 7-401 to 7408.} Section 101. Scope and General Requirements Section 102. Alternative Materials, Methods, and Insulating Systems Section 103. Construction Documents {As in IECC-R} Section 104. Permits and fees Section 105. Inspections Section 106. Notice of Approval {As in IECC-R} Section 107. Validity {As in IECC-R} Section 108. Referenced Standards {As in IECC-R} Section 109. Stop Work Order {Not Adopted; See \u00a7 112.2 of this Chapter} Section 110. Board of Appeals {Not Adopted; See \u00a7113 of this Chapter} Section 111. {Reserved} Section 112. Violations Section 113. Administrative and Judicial Review", "num": "1", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1", "title": "Chapter 1 Scope and Administration", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 101. Scope and General Requirements 101.1 Title. The regulations contained in this Code constitute and are known as the \"Baltimore City Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Residential Provisions\". 101.1.1 References to \"this Code\". Throughout this Part IX-B, all references to \"this Code\" refer to the Baltimore City Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Residential Provisions. 101.2 to 101.5 {As in IECC-R} 101.6 Administration. This Code is administered and enforced by the Department of Housing and Community Development and its Commissioner. Accordingly, in this Code: 1. \"Department\" means the Department of Housing and Community Development, and 2. \"Code Official\" means the Building Official, as defined in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|101", "title": "Section 101. Scope and General Requirements", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/102", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 102. Alternative Materials, Methods, and Insulating Systems 102.1 General. The provisions of this Code are not intended to prevent the installation of any material or to prohibit any method of construction not specifically prescribed by this Code, as long as that alternative has been approved. An alternative material or method may be approved if the Code Official finds in writing that, for the purpose intended: 1. the proposed alternative is satisfactory and complies with the intent of this Code, and 2. the material, method, or work offered is, for the purpose intended at least the equivalent of that prescribed in this Code in quality, strength, effectiveness, fire resistance, durability, and safety. 102.1.1 Above code programs. {As in IECC-R} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "102", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|102", "title": "Section 102. Alternative Materials, Methods, and Insulating Systems", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/102"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/103", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 103. Construction Documents {As in IECC-R} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "103", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|103", "title": "Section 103. Construction Documents\n{As in IECC-R}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/103"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/104", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 104. Permits and fees 104.1 Application for permit. The requirements for obtaining a permit are as set forth in \u00a7 105.3 {\"Application for permit\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 104.2 Expiration of permit. Unless extended, a permit expires as set forth in \u00a7 105.5 {\"Expiration; extension ...\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 104.3 Extension. A permit may be extended as provided in \u00a7 105.5 {\"Expiration; extension ...\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 104.4 Suspension or revocation. The Building Official may suspend or revoke a permit as provided in \u00a7 105.6 {\"Suspension or revocation\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 104.5 Fee schedule. The fee for each permit is as set forth in \u00a7 109 {\"Fees\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "104", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|104", "title": "Section 104. Permits and fees", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/104"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/105", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 105. Inspections 105.1 General. {As in IECC-R} 105.1.1 Code Official's powers and duties. The Code Official must make all of the required inspections or accept reports of inspection by approved agencies or individuals. All reports of these inspections must be in writing and signed by a responsible officer of the approved agency or by the responsible individual. The Code Official may engage any expert opinion that the Code Official considers necessary to report on unusual technical issues that arise. 105.1.2 Right of entry. The Code Official may enter any structure or premises at reasonable times to inspect, subject to constitutional restrictions on unreasonable searches and seizures. If entry is refused or not obtained, the Code Official may pursue recourse as provided by law, including \u00a7 104 {\"...Powers of Building Official\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . 105.2 to 105.7 {As in IECC-R} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "105", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|105", "title": "Section 105. Inspections", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/105"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/106", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 106. Notice of Approval {As in IECC-R} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "106", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|106", "title": "Section 106. Notice of Approval\n{As in IECC-R}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/106"}
