{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/112", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 112. Violations 112.1 Violation penalties. The penalties for a violation of this Code are as provided in \u00a7 114 {\"Violations\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code for a violation of that Code. 112.2 Stop-work orders. The issuance and enforcement of stop-work orders are as provided in \u00a7 115 {\"Stop-Work Order\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "112", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|112", "title": "Section 112. Violations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/112"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/113", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 113. Administrative and Judicial Review 113.1 General. A decision of the Code Official is subject to administrative and judicial review as provided in the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "113", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|1|113", "title": "Section 113. Administrative and Judicial Review", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/113"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 2 Definitions Section 201. General Section 202. General Definitions", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|2", "title": "Chapter 2 Definitions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 201. General 201.1 Scope. {As in IECC-R} 201.2 Interchangeability. {As in IECC-R} 201.3 Terms defined in other codes. If a term is not defined in this Code and is defined in the Baltimore City Building Code or in one or another of the standards and codes listed in \u00a7 101.4 {\"Referenced Codes\"} of the Baltimore City Building Code , the term has the meaning given to it in that code or standard. 201.4 Terms not defined. {As in IECC-R} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|2|201", "title": "Section 201. General", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 202. General Definitions 202.1 General. Except as provided in \u00a7 202.2 of this Code, terms that are used in this Code and defined in the International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Commercial Provisions (2021 Edition) have the meanings given in the International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Commercial Provisions (2021 Edition). 202.2 Supplemental definitions. Notwithstanding any different definition in the International Energy Conservation Code \u2013 Commercial Provisions, the following terms have the meanings given in this \u00a7 202.2. 202.2.1 Building. \"Building\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . 202.2.2 Code official. \"Code official\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 101.6 of this Code. 202.2.3 May not, etc. \"May not\", \"must not\", and \"no ... may\" are each mandatory negative terms used to establish a prohibition. 202.2.4 Must/shall. \"Must\" and \"shall\" are each mandatory terms used to express a requirement or to impose a duty. 202.2.5 Occupancy. \"Occupancy\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . 202.2.6 Premises. \"Premises\" has the meaning stated in \u00a7 202.2 of the Baltimore City Building Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|IX-B|2|202", "title": "Section 202. General Definitions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/IX-B/3", "_type": "page"}}
