{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 901 to 904. {As in IRC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "901 to 904", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|III|9|901to904", "title": "Sections 901 to 904. {As in IRC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/901to904"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/905", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 905. Requirements for Roof Coverings 905.1 to 905.17 {As in IRC} 905.18 Reflectance. Roof Coverings over conditioned spaces on low-slope roofs (roof slope &lt; 2:12) on newly constructed buildings and additions to existing buildings shall have a minimum 3-year-aged solar reflective index of 78, as determined by the Cool Roof Rating Council. Exceptions: 1. An addition to a roof that supports living vegetation and includes a synthetic, high quality waterproof membrane, drainage layer, soil layer, and lightweight medium plants. 2. Roof areas used as outdoor recreation space by the occupants of the building. 3. An area including and adjacent to rooftop photovoltaic and solar thermal equipment, totaling not more than 3 times the area that is covered with photovoltaic and solar thermal equipment. 4. Limited roof areas as determined by regulations promulgated by the department of housing &amp; community development. 5. A roof, the area of which is less than 3% of the gross floor area of the building. 905.18.1 Conflicts. In the event of a conflict between \u00a7 905.18 of this Code and City Code Article 6 {\"Historical and Architectural Preservation\"} , City Code Article 6 {\"Historical and Architectural Preservation\"} prevails. ( Ord. 24-341 ; Ord. 23-252.)", "num": "905", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|III|9|905", "title": "Section 905. Requirements for Roof Coverings", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/905"}
