{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/V/14", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 14 Heating and Cooling Equipment and Appliances Section 1401. General Sections 1402 to 1410. {As in IRC} Section 1411. Heating and Cooling Equipment Section 1412. Absorption Cooling Equipment {As in IRC} Section 1413. Evaporate Cooling Equipment Sections 1414 to 1415. {As in IRC}", "num": "14", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|14", "title": "Chapter 14 Heating and Cooling Equipment and Appliances", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/V/14"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1401", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1401. General 1401.1 to 1401.4 {As in IRC} 1401.5 Flood hazard. In flood hazard areas, heating and cooling equipment and appliances must be located and installed in accordance with the Floodplain Management Code. ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1401", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|14|1401", "title": "Section 1401. General", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1401"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1402to1410", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Sections 1402 to 1410. {As in IRC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1402 to 1410", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|14|1402to1410", "title": "Sections 1402 to 1410. {As in IRC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1402to1410"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1411", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1411. Heating and Cooling Equipment 1411.1 to 1411.2 {As in IRC} 1411.3 Condensate disposal. {As in IRC} 1411.3.1 Auxiliary and secondary drain systems. {As in IRC} 1411.3.2 Drain pipe materials and sizes. Components of the condensate disposal system must be cast iron, galvanized steel, copper, polyethylene, ABS, CPVC, or PVC pipe or tubing. All components must be selected for the pressure and temperature rating of the installation. Condensate waste and drain line size may not be less than \u00be- inch (19 mm) internal diameter and may not decrease in size from the drain pan connection to the place of condensate disposal. Where the drain pipes from more than one unit are manifolded together for condensate drainage, the pipe or tubing must be sized in accordance with an approved method. All horizontal sections of drain piping must be installed in uniform alignment at a uniform slope. 1411.3.3 Drain line maintenance. {As in IRC} 1411.3.4 Appliances, equipment, and insulation in pans. {As in IRC} 1411.4 to 1411.8 {As in IRC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1411", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|14|1411", "title": "Section 1411. Heating and Cooling Equipment", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1411"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1412", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1412. Absorption Cooling Equipment {As in IRC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1412", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|14|1412", "title": "Section 1412. Absorption Cooling Equipment\n{As in IRC}", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1412"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1413", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 1413. Evaporate Cooling Equipment 1413.1 General. {As in IRC} 1413.2 Protection of potable water. The potable water system must be protected from backflow in accordance with the International Plumbing Code . ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "1413", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|14|1413", "title": "Section 1413. Evaporate Cooling Equipment", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/1413"}
