{"body": "Baltimore City Code Chapter 22 Special Piping and Storage Systems Section 2201. Oil Tanks Sections 2202 to 2204. {As in IRC}", "num": "22", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|22", "title": "Chapter 22 Special Piping and Storage Systems", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/V/22"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/2201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Section 2201. Oil Tanks 2201.1 Materials. {As in IRC} 2201.2 Above-ground tanks. {As in IRC} 2201.2.1 Tanks within buildings. {As in IRC} 2201.2.2 Outside above-ground tanks. {As in IRC} Exception: If the 5-feet minimum distance from an adjoining property line cannot be met, the Building Official will determine the location of the tank. 2201.3 to 2201.5 {As in IRC} 2201.6 Flood-resistant installation. In flood hazard areas, tanks must be installed at or above the elevation required by the Floodplain Management Code or as otherwise allowed by the Floodplain Management Code. 2201.7 Tanks abandoned or removed. {As in IRC} ( Ord. 24-341 .)", "num": "2201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|building-codes|X|V|22|2201", "title": "Section 2201. Oil Tanks", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/building-codes/X/2201"}
