{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 1-103. Department. \"Department\" means the Baltimore City Department of Health. (Ord. 22-125; Ord. 99-548.)", "num": "1-103", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|1|1-103", "title": "\u00a7 1-103. Department.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-103"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-104", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 1-104. Physician. \"Physician\" means an individual authorized by law to practice medicine in the State of Maryland. (Ord. 22-125; Ord. 99-548.)", "num": "1-104", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|1|1-104", "title": "\u00a7 1-104. Physician.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-104"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-105", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 1-105. Police officer. \"Police officer\" includes, to the extent of that individual's authority, any individual authorized to act as a Special Enforcement Officer under City Code Article 19, \u00a7 71-1 {\"Special Enforcement Officers \u2014 Appointment; duties\"} . (Ord. 22-125; Ord. 99-548.)", "num": "1-105", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|1|1-105", "title": "\u00a7 1-105. Police officer.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-105"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1/2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 2 Rules of Interpretation \u00a7 1-201. In general. \u00a7 1-202. Conflicting provisions. \u00a7 1-203. Mail. Editor's Notes Ord. 22-125 amended this subtitle to delete several rules of interpretation that were superseded by uniform Code-wide rules codified in the newly enacted General Provisions Article . The sections remaining in this subtitle have been renumbered by authority of Section 2 of Ord. 22-125. For the text of all of the Code-wide rules of interpretation, see General Provisions Article , \u00a7\u00a7 1-201 (In general), 1-203 (Gender), 1-204 (Mandatory, prohibitory, and permissive terms), 1-205 (Singular and plural), 1-208 (Captions or headers), 1-209 (Editor\u2019s or Revisor\u2019s Notes), 1-211 (Effect of repeal or amendment of statute), 1-212 (References to other laws), 1-214 (Severability), and 1-301 et seq. (Time Computations).", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|2", "title": "Subtitle 2 Rules of Interpretation", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 1-201. In general. In interpreting and applying this article , the following rules of interpretation apply: (1) those contained in Subtitles 2 and 3 of the City Code's General Provisions Article ; and (2) any additional rules contained in this subtitle. (Ord. 22-125; Ord. 99-548.)", "num": "1-201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|2|1-201", "title": "\u00a7 1-201. In general.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 1-202. Conflicting provisions. (a) Article sets minimum requirements. In their interpretation and application, the provisions of this article must be taken to be the minimum requirements for the promotion of the public health, safety, and general welfare. (b) Most restrictive provision governs. If any condition imposed by a provision of this article is either more or less restrictive than a comparable condition imposed by any other provision of this article or by any other law, rule, or regulation of any kind, the condition that is the more restrictive governs. (Ord. 22-125; Ord. 99-548.)", "num": "1-202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|2|1-202", "title": "\u00a7 1-202. Conflicting provisions.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-203", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 1-203. Mail. Whenever this article requires the use of \"registered mail\" or \"certified mail\", either method may be used. (Ord. 22-125; Ord. 99-548.)", "num": "1-203", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|health|1|2|1-203", "title": "\u00a7 1-203. Mail.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/health/1-203"}
