{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 14-25. Walters Bath House and Engine House # 10. Walters Bath House and Engine House # 10, 906 Washington Boulevard, the property being further described as follows: Beginning for the same at the point formed by the intersection of the north side of Washington Boulevard and the west side of Callendar Street and running thence binding on the north side of said Washington Boulevard, Westerly 61.5 feet, more or less, to intersect the line of the west face of the west wall of the building situate on the adjacent lot; thence binding in part on the west face of the west wall of said building, in part on the line of the west face of the west wall of said building if projected northerly and in all, Northerly 101 feet, more or less, to intersect the south side of Clifford Street; thence binding on the south side of said Clifford Street, Easterly 61.5 feet, more or less, to the west side of said Callendar Street and thence binding on the west side of said Callendar Street, Southerly 101 feet, more or less, to the place of beginning, the property being further described as Block 0847A, Lot 026. (Ord. 15-408; Ord. 02-315; Ord. 86-851.) Prior Codifications 2000, art. 6, \u00a710-25 City Code, 1976/83, art. 1, \u00a740(ff)(79)", "num": "14-25", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|6|14|14-25", "title": "\u00a7 14-25. Walters Bath House and Engine House # 10.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/6/14-25"}
