{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-601", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-601. In general. The Detached and Semi-Detached Residential Zoning Districts are also subject to the standards listed in this subtitle. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-601", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-601", "title": "\u00a7 8-601. In general.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-601"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-602", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-602. Accessory structures and uses. Standards governing accessory structures and uses are set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 5 {\"Accessory Structures and Uses\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-602", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-602", "title": "\u00a7 8-602. Accessory structures and uses.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-602"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-603", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-603. Site development. On-site development standards are set forth in Title 15 {\"Site Development Standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-603", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-603", "title": "\u00a7 8-603. Site development.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-603"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-604", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-604. Off-street parking and loading. Standards governing off-street parking and loading are set forth in Title 16 {\"Off-Street Parking and Loading\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-604", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-604", "title": "\u00a7 8-604. Off-street parking and loading.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-604"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-605", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-605. Design standards. All developments of the type described in \u00a7 4-405 {\"Design Review: Applicability\"} of this Code must comply with the applicable design standards required by the Baltimore City Design Manual. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-605", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-605", "title": "\u00a7 8-605. Design standards.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-605"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-606", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-606. Landscaping and screening. All landscaping and screening must comply with the requirements of the Baltimore City Landscape Manual. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-606", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-606", "title": "\u00a7 8-606. Landscaping and screening.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-606"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-607", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-607. Signs. Standards governing signs are set forth in Title 17 {\"Signs\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-607", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-607", "title": "\u00a7 8-607. Signs.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-607"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-608", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 8-608. Temporary uses. Standards governing temporary uses are set forth in Title 14, Subtitle 4 {\"Temporary-Use Standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "8-608", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|8|6|8-608", "title": "\u00a7 8-608. Temporary uses.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/8-608"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Title 9 Rowhouse and Multi-Family Residential Districts Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title \u00a7\u00a7 9-101 \u2013 9-101 Subtitle 2 District Descriptions \u00a7\u00a7 9-201 \u2013 9-206 Subtitle 3 Use Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 9-301 \u2013 9-301 Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 9-401 \u2013 9-403 Subtitles 5 and 6 [Reserved] Subtitle 7 Residential Conversions \u00a7\u00a7 9-701 \u2013 9-703 Subtitle 8 Other Applicable Standards \u00a7\u00a7 9-801 \u2013 9-808", "num": "9", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9", "title": "Title 9 Rowhouse and Multi-Family Residential Districts", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title \u00a7 9-101. Purpose.", "num": "1", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|1", "title": "Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-101. Purpose. The purpose of this title is to set out the use regulations and the bulk and yard regulations for Rowhouse and Multi-Family Residential Districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|1|9-101", "title": "\u00a7 9-101. Purpose.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 2 District Descriptions \u00a7 9-201. R-5 Transitional Residential District. \u00a7 9-202. R-6 Garden Rowhouse Residential District. \u00a7 9-203. R-7 Mixed Residential District. \u00a7 9-204. R-8 Rowhouse Residential District. \u00a7 9-205. R-9 Multi-Family Residential District. \u00a7 9-206. R-10 High-Density Residential District.", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2", "title": "Subtitle 2 District Descriptions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-201. R-5 Transitional Residential District. (a) Neighborhoods. The R-5 Transitional Residential Zoning District is intended for those areas that facilitate a transition from primarily single-family neighborhoods to neighborhoods that contain a wider mix of housing types. (b) Housing types. The R-5 District is meant to accommodate single-family units in both detached and semi-detached dwellings, rowhouse developments, and limited low-rise multi-family garden apartment developments of a moderate density. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2|9-201", "title": "\u00a7 9-201. R-5 Transitional Residential District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-202. R-6 Garden Rowhouse Residential District. (a) Neighborhoods. The R-6 Garden Rowhouse Residential Zoning District is intended for primarily low density rowhouse neighborhoods that reflect a naturalistic environment typified by open and landscaped front yards of buildings that are set back and that contain stoops and porches oriented to those yards. (b) Housing types. The R-6 District is meant to accommodate single-family units in both detached and semi-detached dwellings, rowhouse developments, and multi-family developments of a moderate density. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2|9-202", "title": "\u00a7 9-202. R-6 Garden Rowhouse Residential District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-203", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-203. R-7 Mixed Residential District. (a) Neighborhoods. The R-7 Mixed Residential Zoning District is intended for those areas that offer a diverse range of housing types. Development in this district accommodates a transition between naturalistic and urban residential settings. (b) Housing types. The R-7 District is meant to accommodate a diverse range of housing types, including detached and semi-detached dwellings, rowhouse developments, and multi-family developments of a larger scale than found in the more restrictive residential districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-203", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2|9-203", "title": "\u00a7 9-203. R-7 Mixed Residential District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-203"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-204", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-204. R-8 Rowhouse Residential District. (a) Neighborhoods. The R-8 Rowhouse Residential Zoning District is intended to accommodate and maintain the traditional form of urban rowhouse development typical of many of the City's inner neighborhoods, which contain continuous, block-long rowhouse development built to or only modestly set back from the street. (b) Housing types. Although rowhouse is the predominant housing type, this district also accommodates other residential types, of a similar density, including detached and semi-detached dwellings, and multi-family developments of a larger scale than found in more restrictive zoning districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-204", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2|9-204", "title": "\u00a7 9-204. R-8 Rowhouse Residential District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-204"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-205", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-205. R-9 Multi-Family Residential District. (a) Neighborhoods. The R-9 Multi-Family Residential Zoning District is intended for those areas with significant green space surrounding development, particularly higher density housing and non-residential uses. (b) Housing types. The R-9 District contains a mix of higher density, but predominantly mid-rise, housing types. Permitted housing types include single-family homes, both detached and semi-detached, rowhouse developments, and multi-family developments, all with significant front yard open space. Characteristic of this district are multi-family developments sited with significant front yard open space and rowhouse developments with open space both along the perimeter of the site and within the development. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-205", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2|9-205", "title": "\u00a7 9-205. R-9 Multi-Family Residential District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-205"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-206", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-206. R-10 High-Density Residential District. The R-10 High-Density Residential Zoning District is intended for areas of significant density accommodated in concentrated high rise and rowhouse development environments. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-206", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|2|9-206", "title": "\u00a7 9-206. R-10 High-Density Residential District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-206"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 3 Use Regulations \u00a7 9-301. As listed in Table 9-301.", "num": "3", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|3", "title": "Subtitle 3 Use Regulations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-301", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-301. As listed in Table 9-301. Only those uses of land listed in Table 9-301: Rowhouse and Multi-Family Residential Districts \u2013 Permitted and Conditional Uses are allowed within these zoning districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-301", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|3|9-301", "title": "\u00a7 9-301. As listed in Table 9-301.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-301"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations \u00a7 9-401. In general. \u00a7 9-402. Measurement methodologies; Exceptions, etc. \u00a7 9-403. Setback reduction for courtyard design.", "num": "4", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|4", "title": "Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-401", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-401. In general. Table 9-401: Rowhouse and Multi-Family Residential Districts \u2013 Bulk and Yard Regulations sets forth the applicable bulk and yard regulations for these zoning districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-401", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|4|9-401", "title": "\u00a7 9-401. In general.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-401"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-402", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-402. Measurement methodologies; Exceptions, etc. (a) Measurement methodologies. Measurement methodologies are as set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 3 {\"Measurement Methodologies\"} of this Code. (b) Exceptions and requirements. Exceptions and requirements are as set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 4 {\"Exceptions and Requirements\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-402", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|4|9-402", "title": "\u00a7 9-402. Measurement methodologies; Exceptions, etc.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-402"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-403", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-403. Setback reduction for courtyard design. (a) In general. Multi-family dwellings designed with a courtyard are permitted a reduction of the front yard requirement. (b) Requirements. Front yards may be reduced for courtyard building design as long as: (1) no more than 75% of the building's frontage maintains a minimum front yard of 15 feet; (2) the remaining frontage meets the minimum required front yard or 30 feet, whichever is greater; and (3) those portions of the courtyard building located at a reduced front yard are evenly spaced or within 10% of even spacing. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-403", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|4|9-403", "title": "\u00a7 9-403. Setback reduction for courtyard design.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-403"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/5and6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitles 5 and 6 [Reserved]", "num": "5 and 6", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|5and6", "title": "Subtitles 5 and 6 [Reserved]", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/5and6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/7", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 7 Residential Conversions \u00a7 9-701. Where allowed. \u00a7 9-702. Design review. \u00a7 9-703. Conversion standards.", "num": "7", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|7", "title": "Subtitle 7 Residential Conversions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/7"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-701", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-701. Where allowed. In the Residence Districts, the conversion of a single-family dwelling to a multi-family dwelling is allowed only in the R-7, R-8, R-9, and R-10 Districts, subject to: (1) the requirements of this subtitle; and (2) in the R-7 and R-8 Districts, conditional-use approval by Ordinance of the Mayor and City Council. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-701", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|7|9-701", "title": "\u00a7 9-701. Where allowed.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-701"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-702", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-702. Design review. (a) In general. Design review approval is required if exterior modifications are proposed. (b) Construction drawings and plans. As part of the submittal for design review, construction drawings and plans that describe the proposed conversion in detail are required. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-702", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|7|9-702", "title": "\u00a7 9-702. Design review.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-702"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-703", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-703. Conversion standards. (a) In general. All conversions must meet the standards set forth in this section. (b) Existing dwelling. (1) The existing dwelling must be: (i) a structure originally constructed as a single-family dwelling; and (ii) 1,500 square feet or more in gross floor area. (2) For purposes of this subsection, gross floor area does not include any basement area. (c) GFA per dwelling unit. The converted dwelling must meet the following gross floor area per unit type: (1) 1-bedroom unit: 750 square feet. (2) 2-bedroom unit: 1,000 square feet. (3) 3- or more bedroom unit: 1,250 square feet. (d) Bulk and yard regulations. The dwelling must continue to conform to the applicable bulk and yard regulations, including lot area per dwelling unit, for the district in which the building is located. (e) Occupancy regulations. No residential conversion may violate any dwelling unit occupancy regulations or restrictions of the City Code. (f) Off-street parking. At least 1 off-street parking space must be provided for each dwelling unit. (g) Residential character. Following the conversion, the exterior of the dwelling must retain its existing residential character. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-703", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|7|9-703", "title": "\u00a7 9-703. Conversion standards.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-703"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/8", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 8 Other Applicable Standards \u00a7 9-801. In general. \u00a7 9-802. Accessory structures and uses. \u00a7 9-803. Site development. \u00a7 9-804. Off-street parking and loading. \u00a7 9-805. Design standards. \u00a7 9-806. Landscaping and screening. \u00a7 9-807. Signs. \u00a7 9-808. Temporary uses.", "num": "8", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8", "title": "Subtitle 8 Other Applicable Standards", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9/8"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-801", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-801. In general. The Rowhouse and Multi-Family Residential Zoning Districts are also subject to the standards listed in this subtitle. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-801", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-801", "title": "\u00a7 9-801. In general.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-801"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-802", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-802. Accessory structures and uses. Standards governing accessory structures and uses are set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 5 {\"Accessory Structures and Uses\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-802", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-802", "title": "\u00a7 9-802. Accessory structures and uses.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-802"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-803", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-803. Site development. On-site development standards are set forth in Title 15 {\"Site Development Standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-803", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-803", "title": "\u00a7 9-803. Site development.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-803"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-804", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-804. Off-street parking and loading. Standards governing off-street parking and loading are set forth in Title 16 {\"Off-Street Parking and Loading\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-804", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-804", "title": "\u00a7 9-804. Off-street parking and loading.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-804"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-805", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-805. Design standards. All developments of the type described in \u00a7 4-405 {\"Design Review: Applicability\"} of this Code must comply with the applicable design standards required by the Baltimore City Design Manual. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-805", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-805", "title": "\u00a7 9-805. Design standards.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-805"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-806", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-806. Landscaping and screening. All landscaping and screening must comply with the requirements of the Baltimore City Landscape Manual. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-806", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-806", "title": "\u00a7 9-806. Landscaping and screening.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-806"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-807", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-807. Signs. Standards governing signs are set forth in Title 17 {\"Signs\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-807", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-807", "title": "\u00a7 9-807. Signs.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-807"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-808", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 9-808. Temporary uses. Standards governing temporary uses are set forth in Title 14, Subtitle 4 {\"Temporary-Use Standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "9-808", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|9|8|9-808", "title": "\u00a7 9-808. Temporary uses.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/9-808"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Title 10 Commercial Districts Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title \u00a7\u00a7 10-101 \u2013 10-101 Subtitle 2 District Descriptions \u00a7\u00a7 10-201 \u2013 10-207 Subtitle 3 Use Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 10-301 \u2013 10-301 Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 10-401 \u2013 10-402 Subtitle 5 Design Standards for C-5 District \u00a7\u00a7 10-501 \u2013 10-504 Subtitle 6 Other Applicable Standards \u00a7\u00a7 10-601 \u2013 10-609", "num": "10", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10", "title": "Title 10 Commercial Districts", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title \u00a7 10-101. Purpose.", "num": "1", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|1", "title": "Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-101. Purpose. The purpose of this title is to set out the use regulations and the bulk and yard regulations for Commercial Zoning Districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|1|10-101", "title": "\u00a7 10-101. Purpose.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 2 District Descriptions \u00a7 10-201. C-1 Neighborhood Business District. \u00a7 10-202. C-1-E Neighborhood Business and Entertainment District. \u00a7 10-203. C-1-VC Neighborhood Business District (Village Center). \u00a7 10-204. C-2 Community Commercial District. \u00a7 10-205. C-3 General Commercial District. \u00a7 10-206. C-4 Heavy Commercial District. \u00a7 10-207. C-5 Downtown District.", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2", "title": "Subtitle 2 District Descriptions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-201. C-1 Neighborhood Business District. (a) Areas for which intended. The C-1 Neighborhood Business Zoning District is intended for areas of commercial clusters or pedestrian-oriented corridors of commercial uses that serve the immediate neighborhood. (b) Standards. The C-1 District standards are crafted to: (1) ensure compatibility between neighboring residential and commercial uses; (2) maintain the proper scale of commercial use; and (3) address the unique issues related to smaller commercial sites. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-201", "title": "\u00a7 10-201. C-1 Neighborhood Business District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-202. C-1-E Neighborhood Business and Entertainment District. (a) Areas for which intended. The C-1-E Neighborhood Business and Entertainment Zoning District is intended for areas of commercial clusters or pedestrian-oriented corridors of commercial uses that serve the immediate neighborhood and allow for clustering of entertainment uses. (b) Standards. The C-1-E District standards are crafted to: (1) ensure compatibility among neighboring residential, commercial, and entertainment uses; (2) maintain the proper scale of commercial use; and (3) address the unique issues related to smaller commercial sites. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-202", "title": "\u00a7 10-202. C-1-E Neighborhood Business and Entertainment District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-203", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-203. C-1-VC Neighborhood Business District (Village Center). (a) Areas for which intended. The C-1-VC Neighborhood Business Zoning District (Village Center) is intended for areas of commercial clusters or pedestrian-oriented corridors of commercial uses that serve the immediate neighborhood in a low scale and with a mix of attached and detached structures. (b) Standards. The C-1-VC District standards are crafted to: (1) ensure compatibility between neighboring residential and commercial uses; (2) maintain the proper scale of commercial use; and (3) address the unique issues related to small commercial sites. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-203", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-203", "title": "\u00a7 10-203. C-1-VC Neighborhood Business District (Village Center).", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-203"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-204", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-204. C-2 Community Commercial District. (a) Areas for which intended. The C-2 Community Commercial Zoning District is intended for areas of small to medium-scale commercial use, typically located along urban corridors, that are designed to accommodate pedestrians and, in some instances, automobiles. (b) Standards. The C-2 District standards are crafted to: (1) ensure compatibility among neighboring residential, commercial, and entertainment uses; (2) maintain the proper scale of commercial use; and (3) maintain a balance between high traffic volume and pedestrian circulation. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-204", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-204", "title": "\u00a7 10-204. C-2 Community Commercial District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-204"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-205", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-205. C-3 General Commercial District. (a) Areas for which intended. (1) The C-3 General Commercial Zoning District is intended for more intensive commercial uses and key commercial nodes that require additional controls, particularly for shopping centers and larger retail establishments. (2) The C-3 District accommodates larger developments that may require significant parking, such as shopping centers and large-scale mixed-use development. (b) Standards. The C-3 District standards are crafted to: (1) ensure compatibility among neighboring residential, commercial, and entertainment uses; (2) ensure high quality pedestrian connections between public sidewalks and business entrances; and (3) create store fronts that are oriented towards streets and other public ways. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-205", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-205", "title": "\u00a7 10-205. C-3 General Commercial District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-205"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-206", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-206. C-4 Heavy Commercial District. (a) Areas for which intended. The C-4 Heavy Commercial Zoning District is intended for areas of more intense commercial use that are generally not appropriate for lower intensity commercial districts, including uses related to motor vehicles and those that might require outdoor storage. (b) Standards. Because of the impacts from more intensive commercial uses, the standards for this district ensure that setbacks, buffering, and site development controls are in place to mitigate negative impacts on neighboring uses. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-206", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-206", "title": "\u00a7 10-206. C-4 Heavy Commercial District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-206"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-207", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-207. C-5 Downtown District. (a) Areas for which intended. The C-5 Downtown Zoning District is intended for Baltimore's Downtown and accommodates a wide range of uses normally associated with the downtown of a major city. (b) Standards. The C-5 District standards are crafted to: (1) maintain or improve the pedestrian environment; (2) ensure that new construction is compatible with existing development; and (3) develop a greener downtown. (c) Subdistricts. (1) In general. In order to address the different character areas that make up Downtown, the C-5 District is divided into the following subdistricts, for which varied bulk and yard regulations are provided to recognize the different physical characteristics of Downtown. (2) C-5-DC Downtown Core Subdistrict. (i) The purpose of the C-5-DC Downtown Core Subdistrict is to establish these standards for structures located within the majority of Downtown. (ii) The standards recognize that this subdistrict is to be the most intensely developed portion of Downtown and is to be predominately pedestrian-oriented in nature. (3) C-5-IH Inner Harbor Subdistrict. (i) The purpose of the C-5-IH Inner Harbor Subdistrict is to establish these standards for structures located adjacent to and facing the Inner Harbor. (ii) The standards recognize that development within this subdistrict is to be oriented to the Inner Harbor waterfront and be predominantly pedestrian-oriented and mixed-use. (4) C-5-DE Downtown East Subdistrict. (i) The purpose of the C-5-DE Downtown East Subdistrict is to establish these standards for structures within a high intensity waterfront-oriented area. (ii) The standards recognize that this area is to contain intense levels of development to create a high density, walkable, mixed-use environment where careful placement of structures affords visual access to the waterfront as well as pedestrian access within. (iii) Because this subdistrict is adjacent to lower density neighborhoods of historic and traditional character, the intensity and height of development on the periphery of the subdistrict are intended to provide a transition between the core of this subdistrict and the adjacent neighborhoods. (5) C-5-HT Downtown Historic and Traditional Subdistrict. (i) The purpose of the C-5-HT Downtown Historic and Traditional Subdistrict is to establish these standards for structures in an area of Downtown containing substantial historic and traditional architecture that has evolved since the founding of the City. (ii) Given the character of that development, this district is designed to require relatively low heights and the use of materials that reflect the existing development context. (6) C-5-TO Downtown Traditional Office Subdistrict. The purpose of the C-5-TO Downtown Traditional Office Subdistrict is: (i) to establish these standards for structures in an area that primarily consists of early 20 th Century office development; and (ii) to seek to maintain a distinctive and desirable environment. (7) C-5-HS Howard Street Mixed-Use Subdistrict. The purpose of the C-5-HS Howard Street Mixed-Use Subdistrict is to establish these standards for structures to facilitate a transition between the intensive development of the Downtown core and the more modest-scale development found in adjacent, primarily residential environments. (8) C-5-G Government Center Subdistrict. (i) The purpose of the C-5-G Government Center Subdistrict is to establish these standards for structures that reflect the scale of major governmental buildings located within the district. (ii) The intent is to ensure that future development reflects the existing scale of development and maintains critical views of these public buildings from the adjacent areas. ( Ord. 24-319 ; Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-207", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|2|10-207", "title": "\u00a7 10-207. C-5 Downtown District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-207"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 3 Use Regulations \u00a7 10-301. As listed in Table 10-301.", "num": "3", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|3", "title": "Subtitle 3 Use Regulations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-301", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-301. As listed in Table 10-301. Only those uses of land listed in Table 10-301: Commercial Districts \u2013 Permitted and Conditional Uses are allowed within these zoning districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-301", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|3|10-301", "title": "\u00a7 10-301. As listed in Table 10-301.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-301"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations \u00a7 10-401. In general. \u00a7 10-402. Measurement methodologies; Exceptions, etc.", "num": "4", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|4", "title": "Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-401", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-401. In general. Table 10-401: Commercial Districts \u2013 Bulk and Yard Regulations sets forth the applicable bulk and yard regulations for these zoning districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-401", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|4|10-401", "title": "\u00a7 10-401. In general.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-401"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-402", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-402. Measurement methodologies; Exceptions, etc. (a) Measurement methodologies. Measurement methodologies are as set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 3 {\"Measurement Methodologies\"} of this Code. (b) Exceptions and requirements. Exceptions and requirements are as set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 4 {\"Exceptions and Requirements\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-402", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|4|10-402", "title": "\u00a7 10-402. Measurement methodologies; Exceptions, etc.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-402"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 5 Design Standards for C-5 District \u00a7 10-501. Harbor promenade. \u00a7 10-502. Open-space plazas. \u00a7 10-503. Parking and access. \u00a7 10-504. View protection.", "num": "5", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|5", "title": "Subtitle 5 Design Standards for C-5 District", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-501", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-501. Harbor promenade. Within certain areas of the C-5-DC, C-5-IH, and C-5-DE Subdistricts, a harbor promenade is required. (The applicable areas are shown on the zoning map for the Waterfront Overlay Zoning Districts.) New development in these areas must comply with Title 12, Subtitle 9 {\"Waterfront Overlay Zoning Districts\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-501", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|5|10-501", "title": "\u00a7 10-501. Harbor promenade.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-501"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-502", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-502. Open-space plazas. (a) Permitted in C-5 District. Public open-space plazas are permitted within the C-5 District. (b) Design requirements. Open-space plazas must comply with the following design requirements: (1) a plaza must be designed to be accessible from adjoining buildings and for generally unobstructed pedestrian circulation throughout the plaza; and (2) visibility into the plaza may not be entirely blocked by structures. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-502", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|5|10-502", "title": "\u00a7 10-502. Open-space plazas.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-502"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-503", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-503. Parking and access. (a) District exempt from parking requirements. The C-5 District is exempt from the parking requirements of this Code. (b) New curb cuts. New curb cuts are prohibited on primary streets ( see Design Manual). (c) Along Pratt Street. Along Pratt Street: (1) parking garages as principal uses are prohibited; (2) vehicle entries to parking garages are prohibited; and (3) all parking garages must be faced with active ground-floor uses, whether residential or non-residential. (Ord. 22-181; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-503", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|5|10-503", "title": "\u00a7 10-503. Parking and access.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-503"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-504", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-504. View protection. (a) Skyways, street bridges prohibited. Except as provided in subsection (b) of this section, skyways and street bridges are prohibited in the C-5 District. (b) Exception for hospital uses For hospital uses, a skyway or street bridge is allowed, subject to conditional use approval from the Board of Municipal and Zoning Appeals. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-504", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|5|10-504", "title": "\u00a7 10-504. View protection.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-504"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 6 Other Applicable Standards \u00a7 10-601. In general. \u00a7 10-602. Accessory structures and uses. \u00a7 10-603. Site development. \u00a7 10-604. Off-street parking and loading. \u00a7 10-605. Design standards. \u00a7 10-606. Landscaping and screening. \u00a7 10-607. Signs. \u00a7 10-608. Temporary uses. \u00a7 10-609. Residential conversions.", "num": "6", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6", "title": "Subtitle 6 Other Applicable Standards", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10/6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-601", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-601. In general. The Commercial Zoning Districts are also subject to the standards listed in this subtitle. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-601", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-601", "title": "\u00a7 10-601. In general.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-601"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-602", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-602. Accessory structures and uses. Standards governing accessory structures and uses are set forth in Title 15, Subtitle 5 {\"Accessory Structures and Uses\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-602", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-602", "title": "\u00a7 10-602. Accessory structures and uses.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-602"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-603", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-603. Site development. On-site development standards are set forth in Title 15 {\"Site Development Standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-603", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-603", "title": "\u00a7 10-603. Site development.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-603"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-604", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-604. Off-street parking and loading. Standards governing off-street parking and loading are set forth in Title 16 {\"Off-Street Parking and Loading\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-604", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-604", "title": "\u00a7 10-604. Off-street parking and loading.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-604"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-605", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-605. Design standards. All developments of the type described in \u00a7 4-405 {\"Design Review: Applicability\"} of this Code must comply with the applicable design standards required by the Baltimore City Design Manual. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-605", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-605", "title": "\u00a7 10-605. Design standards.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-605"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-606", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-606. Landscaping and screening. All landscaping and screening must comply with the requirements of the Baltimore City Landscape Manual. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-606", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-606", "title": "\u00a7 10-606. Landscaping and screening.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-606"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-607", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-607. Signs. Standards governing signs are set forth in Title 17 {\"Signs\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-607", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-607", "title": "\u00a7 10-607. Signs.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-607"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-608", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-608. Temporary uses. Standards governing temporary uses are set forth in Title 14, Subtitle 4 {\"Temporary-Use Standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-608", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-608", "title": "\u00a7 10-608. Temporary uses.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-608"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-609", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 10-609. Residential conversions. The conversion of a single-family dwelling to a multi-family dwelling is allowed in the Commercial Zoning Districts, subject to the requirements of \u00a7 9-702 {\"Residential Conversions: Design review\"} and \u00a7 9-703 {\"Residential Conversions: Conversion standards\"} of this Code. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "10-609", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|10|6|10-609", "title": "\u00a7 10-609. Residential conversions.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/10-609"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Title 11 Industrial Districts Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title \u00a7\u00a7 11-101 \u2013 11-101 Subtitle 2 District Descriptions \u00a7\u00a7 11-201 \u2013 11-206 Subtitle 3 Use Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 11-301 \u2013 11-301 Subtitle 4 Bulk and Yard Regulations \u00a7\u00a7 11-401 \u2013 11-402 Subtitle 5 [Reserved] Subtitle 6 Other Applicable Standards \u00a7\u00a7 11-601 \u2013 11-608", "num": "11", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11", "title": "Title 11 Industrial Districts", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11/1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title \u00a7 11-101. Purpose.", "num": "1", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|1", "title": "Subtitle 1 Purpose of Title", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11/1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-101", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-101. Purpose. The purpose of this title is to set out the use regulations and the bulk and yard regulations for Industrial Zoning Districts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-101", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|1|11-101", "title": "\u00a7 11-101. Purpose.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-101"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11/2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code Subtitle 2 District Descriptions \u00a7 11-201. OIC Office-Industrial Campus District. \u00a7 11-202. BSC Bio-Science Campus District. \u00a7 11-203. IMU Industrial Mixed-Use Districts. \u00a7 11-204. I-1 Light Industrial District. \u00a7 11-205. I-2 General Industrial District. \u00a7 11-206. MI Maritime Industrial District.", "num": "2", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2", "title": "Subtitle 2 District Descriptions", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11/2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-201", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-201. OIC Office-Industrial Campus District. (a) In general. (1) Intent. The OIC Office-Industrial Campus Zoning District is intended for developments of large office structures, research and development facilities, and light industrial uses. (2) Minimum size of district. An OIC District must encompass at least 1 acre of land. (b) Standards. The OIC District standards are intended for architecturally coordinated office and industrial structures built in a campus-like atmosphere. (c) Typical uses. Examples of typical OIC District uses include: (1) the international headquarters of a large corporation; (2) large research and development facilities; and (3) office campuses of substantial size. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-201", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2|11-201", "title": "\u00a7 11-201. OIC Office-Industrial Campus District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-201"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-202", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-202. BSC Bio-Science Campus District. (a) In general. (1) Intent. The BSC Bio-Science Campus Zoning District is intended to accommodate bio-science campuses, including supportive uses, and some residential uses. (2) Minimum size of district. A BSC District must encompass at least 1 acre of land. (b) Uses. The BSC District allows: (1) a broad mix of uses, integrating manufacturing, office, and research and development; and (2) additional supportive uses, like limited retail, educational facilities, and some higher density residential uses. (Ord. 17-015; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-202", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2|11-202", "title": "\u00a7 11-202. BSC Bio-Science Campus District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-202"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-203", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-203. IMU Industrial Mixed-Use Districts. (a) Intent. (1) The IMU Industrial Mixed-Use Zoning Districts are intended to encourage the reuse of older industrial buildings for light industrial use, as well as a variety of non-industrial uses. (2) These older industrial buildings are often surrounded by residential and other non-industrial uses, though in many cases they are also transition zones between a heavy industrial area and a major road or a less intense use or district. (b) Types of IMU Districts. (1) 2 types of IMU Districts are established, as follows: (i) one, the IMU-1 District, allows a variety of residential uses, including live-work dwellings; and (ii) the other, the IMU-2 District, prohibits all residential uses. (2) The IMU-1 District is generally for industrial buildings that are adjacent to existing residential buildings, typically rowhouses. (3) The IMU-2 District is generally for industrial buildings that are adjacent to heavier industry, port uses, highways, or truck routes and not residential areas. This district is intended to protect industrial land and truck routes from pressures of residential uses. (c) Floor area requirement for certain uses. (1) In an IMU-1 District, a use other than residential and other than parking must account for a floor area (located anywhere in any building on the same lot) equal to at least 60% of the total ground-floor area of all buildings on the lot, unless otherwise granted a variance by the Board of Municipal and Zoning Appeals. (2) In an IMU-2 District, a use listed in the \"Industrial Use Category\" of Table 11-301 {\"Industrial Districts \u2013 Permitted and Conditional Uses\"} as allowed for an IMU-2 District must account for a floor area (located anywhere in any building on the same lot) equal to at least 50% of the total ground floor area of all buildings on the lot, unless otherwise granted a variance by the Board of Municipal and Zoning Appeals. (Ord. 22-181; Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-203", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2|11-203", "title": "\u00a7 11-203. IMU Industrial Mixed-Use Districts.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-203"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-204", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-204. I-1 Light Industrial District. (a) Intent. The I-1 Light Industrial Zoning District is intended to provide for a wide variety of light manufacturing, fabricating, processing, wholesale distributing, and warehousing uses. (b) Light industrial uses. Light industrial uses are enclosed low-intensity, non-nuisance light fabrication and assembly-type manufacturing, with little to no outside impacts. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-204", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2|11-204", "title": "\u00a7 11-204. I-1 Light Industrial District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-204"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-205", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-205. I-2 General Industrial District. (a) Intent. The I-2 General Industrial Zoning District is intended to provide for a wide variety of general manufacturing, fabricating, processing, wholesale distributing, and warehousing uses. (b) Uses. (1) General industrial uses include fabrication, warehousing and assembly-type manufacturing, which may result in some moderate external effects, such as smoke, noise, glare, or vibration, and typically include outdoor storage and related outdoor activities. (2) Commercial uses and outdoor storage of materials are allowed. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-205", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2|11-205", "title": "\u00a7 11-205. I-2 General Industrial District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-205"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-206", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Baltimore City Code \u00a7 11-206. MI Maritime Industrial District. (a) Intent. The MI Maritime Industrial Zoning District is intended to ensure the preservation of deep-water frontage of the Port of Baltimore for maritime industrial uses by delineating an area where maritime shipping and maritime industrial uses can be conducted without the intrusion of non-industrial uses and where investment in maritime infrastructure is encouraged. (b) Nature of uses. The nature of these activities may result in external effects, such as smoke, noise, glare, or vibration, and typically include outdoor storage and related outdoor activities. (Ord. 16-581.)", "num": "11-206", "path": "library|City of Baltimore, Md., Code|32|11|2|11-206", "title": "\u00a7 11-206. MI Maritime Industrial District.", "url": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11-206"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/md/cities/baltimore/code/32/11/3", "_type": "page"}}
